                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is ... soulless.\r\n\r\nTechnically bad, a little bit, it has very limited settings and took me lowering the sound effects volume as a suggestion and ignored it.  Also, some simple dialogue errors like have \"emphasize\" where it was clearly supposed to be \"empathize\".  Missing some basic RPG staples like a quest journal too\r\n\r\nFor my personal tastes, the game had so much working against it.  The plot felt poorly thought out, the characters were anime cliches, the dialogue seemed to press against the fourth wall \"She just cast an S rank spell!\", and there was almost no statistical difference between the party members.  Two are literally no different past the portrait and name.  And somehow past all that it managed to be really boring.\r\n\r\nIt's not the worst thing I've ever played, but it isn't good.  3/10.",
